{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "mq4cs-gpt41-splade", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-1_8", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Stress, such as the kind experienced with a looming deadline, can exacerbate acid reflux symptoms. Stress may lead to habits like overeating or eating quickly, which can increase stomach acid and cause reflux. Additionally, stress can tighten your muscles, including those around your stomach, potentially worsening symptoms.  Regarding over-the-counter (OTC) medications for acid reflux, quite a few are available to provide relief. Antacids like Maalox, Mylanta, Tums, and Gaviscon can offer quick relief by neutralizing stomach acid. H2 receptor antagonists such as famotidine (Pepcid, Zantac 360) and cimetidine (Tagamet) reduce acid production and provide longer relief than antacids. Proton-pump inhibitors (PPIs) such as Prilosec\u00ae, Nexium\u00ae, and Prevacid\u00ae can also be used to block acid production, providing more prolonged relief.  You might consider using these medications to manage symptoms while paying attention to your eating habits, especially during stressful times. However, if symptoms persist, consulting a healthcare provider is advisable.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0044-99-14195:8": 2.6530293812981167, "clueweb22-en0017-96-03792:10": 2.65125856542201, "clueweb22-en0005-31-05925:6": 2.5535074575686134, "clueweb22-en0041-97-07392:7": 2.3145138272780668, "clueweb22-en0016-97-03528:3": 2.2602100963129974, "clueweb22-en0012-13-07696:11": 2.198750004118538, "clueweb22-en0015-45-13434:4": 2.1306089310221052, "clueweb22-en0043-05-13136:7": 1.9489170658247046, "clueweb22-en0040-38-20110:13": 1.9315542875383214, "clueweb22-en0026-80-18810:6": 1.8602710434545098}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I want to stop doom scrolling.", "I have gained weight recently because I stopped exercising for the last 6 months.", "I spend too much time on my phone.", "I want to change my lifestyle."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0044-99-1419