{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "mq4cs-gpt41-splade", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "2-1_7", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Certainly! Liberica beans are distinguished by their unique almond-like shape. In contrast, Excelsa beans are smaller, rounder, and often asymmetrical, averaging about 9mm in length and 6mm in width.  Regarding caffeine content, Excelsa beans generally contain less caffeine than the more common Arabica and Robusta beans. Specifically, the caffeine levels in Excelsa beans range from 0.86 to 1.13 grams per 100 grams. While specific data on Liberica's caffeine content is less well-documented, Excelsa's caffeine content is known to be lower, making it potentially more suitable for those seeking a milder caffeine experience.  If you're interested in experimenting with a new coffee taste, Excelsa's fruity and tart profile might be a refreshing choice, while Liberica can offer a unique mix of floral, fruity, and smoky flavors. Both offer distinct experiences compared to the more common varieties.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0004-97-11464:6": 4.565085180954126, "clueweb22-en0022-85-00226:7": 3.576286564130134, "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:13": 3.37403410047746, "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:12": 3.3541723898957763, "clueweb22-en0004-97-11464:5": 2.8469793244195536, "clueweb22-en0022-85-00226:6": 2.7699161965224777, "clueweb22-en0004-97-11464:4": 2.756546757148457, "clueweb22-en0031-16-17635:9": 2.4353841226426978, "clueweb22-en0020-47-18754:2": 2.4155180649410064, "clueweb22-en0031-16-17635:8": 2.4110733455296454}, "ptkb_provenance": ["Excelsa has recently been reclassified as a type of Liberica coffee because it thrives in the same conditions and grows a similarly tall tree. But the actual coffee it produces is vastly different. It has a much fruitier character than Liberica, with a tart acidity that makes it popular for adding complexity to coffee blends. Excelsa coffee makes up only about 7% of the current coffee market. Still, given its appealing flavor profile and the fact that it is nearly as resilient and productive as Robusta, this seems likely to grow. Much like Robusta, Excelsa coffee has been regarded as poor quality, but this is more due to poor growing and processing practices than the bean itself. With the proper care, Excelsa has the potential to be specialty-grade coffee.", "Liberica beans make up only about 2% of the world's current coffee crop. Once upon a time, this varietal was far more critical after disease wiped out much of the world's Arabica supply. Arabica has since made a comeback, and Liberica production has primarily ceased. However, that may change in the future, as climate change makes it increasingly challenging to produce the more sensitive Arabica plants reliably. Liberica coffee has a unique flavor, pairing floral and fruity notes with a deep smokiness that some describe as woody. It has a full-bodied, reminiscent of Robusta coffee. It's not to everyone's taste, but there are some exceptional Liberica coffees to be had when done right."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0004-97-11464:6": 4.565085180954126, "clueweb22-en0022-85-00226:7": 3.576286564130134, "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:13": 3.37403410047746, "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:12": 3.3541723898957763, "clueweb22-en0004-97-11464:5": 2.8469793244195536, "clueweb22-en0022-85-00226:6": 2.7699161965224777, "clueweb22-en0004-97-11464:4": 2.756546757148457, "clueweb22-en0031-16-17635:9": 2.4353841226426978, "clueweb22-en0020-47-18754:2": 2.4155180649410064, "clueweb22-en0031-16-17635:8": 2.4110733455296454, "clueweb22-en0036-21-16351:4": 2.369496219863743, "clueweb22-en0001-20-10010:19": 2.356854906783054, "clueweb22-en0004-97-11464:7": 2.354202324823812, "clueweb22-en0019-88-13848:4": 2.2993391760543083, "clueweb22-en0036-21-16351:5": 2.2245875156148553, "clueweb22-en0031-65-00073:17": 2.2189603438254872, "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:8": 2.1676995234632273, "clueweb22-en0001-37-16016:10": 2.151813151362598, "clueweb22