{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "mq4cs-gpt41-splade", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-2_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "The jockey, also known as the jockey wheel, refers to one of the two small pulleys in the rear derailleur of your bike. These pulleys guide the chain onto the cassette. The jockey wheels are housed in a cage and typically follow a vertically positioned S-shaped pattern. There are two types of jockey wheels: the guide pulley, which is at the top and closest to the sprockets, and the tension pulley, which is at the bottom. The guide pulley helps to direct the chain onto the correct sprocket when you shift gears. The tension pulley, on the other hand, helps maintain the proper tension in the chain, ensuring smooth operation even when the chainline is not perfectly straight. These components are crucial in the functioning of your bike's drivetrain, helping it compensate for small misalignments and ensuring smooth, reliable shifting.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0032-78-01787:0": 4.8719113395051235, "clueweb22-en0039-65-07416:1": 4.702468535272814, "clueweb22-en0032-78-01787:1": 4.437778158726541, "clueweb22-en0039-65-07416:2": 4.356971599329193, "clueweb22-en0018-20-12295:16": 3.5946790398790296, "clueweb22-en0040-35-09091:5": 3.563941886089329, "clueweb22-en0039-65-07416:3": 3.5633921151583636, "clueweb22-en0017-19-02622:1": 3.349201316232124, "clueweb22-en0018-20-12295:15": 3.2299072873151546, "clueweb22-en0022-23-00873:11": 3.2065559211696013}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I'm a casual bike rider.", "I take my bike in the train and the bus.", "I like biking even in rainy weather and in the forest."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0032-78-01787:0": 4.8719113395051235, "clueweb22-en0039-65-07416:1": 4.702468535272814, "clueweb22-en0032-78-01787:1": 4.437778158726541, "clueweb22-en0039-65-07416:2": 4.356971599329193, "clueweb22-en0018-20-12295:16": 3.5946790398790296, "clueweb22-en0040-35-09091:5": 3.563941886089329, "clueweb22-en0039-