{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "mq4cs-gpt41-splade", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-2_8", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To open your bike chain with a chain breaker tool, follow these steps:  1. **Position the Chain**: Place the chain link you want to open into the chain breaker's groove. Ensure the link is secure in the tool's prongs.  2. **Align the Pin**: Align the chain breaker's metal pin with the chain pin you want to push out. Make sure the pin is centered on the link.  3. **Turn the Handle**: Slowly turn the handle of the chain breaker tool clockwise. This will push the tool's pin into the chain link. Be careful to maintain alignment to avoid damage.  4. **Push the Pin Partially**: Continue turning until the chain pin is pushed far enough that the link can be separated without fully removing the pin, making reassembly easier.  5. **Separate the Link**: Once the pin is sufficiently pushed out, remove the chain from the tool. Wiggle the chain link back and forth to separate it.  After making the necessary adjustments to your chain length using the method you prefer, you can reassemble the chain by aligning the links and pushing the pin back in with the chain breaker.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0027-35-00252:2": 4.588117385844048, "clueweb22-en0031-00-17726:9": 4.496373152173283, "clueweb22-en0027-35-00252:6": 4.403782486801173, "clueweb22-en0027-35-00252:1": 3.9969725216713963, "clueweb22-en0019-70-04653:14": 3.576391643849904, "clueweb22-en0007-76-12829:4": 3.5075601984418188, "clueweb22-en0007-76-12829:5": 3.16314760008568, "clueweb22-en0019-70-04653:13": 2.988495928924745, "clueweb22-en0020-78-15858:11": 2.9086113840276684, "clueweb22-en0020-78-15858:8": 2.868523450126192}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I sometimes get overwhelmed by too many technical choices.", "I'm a casual bike rider.", "I have a small garage that I use as workshop space at home.", "I am not really handy with DIY."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0027-35-00252:2": 4.58